From 47e3833d34ecfb1d2aa850ea7bb3d4f499693d76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil <300208363+calicopizzadelivery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:32:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] System: an AirPlay page

Settings > System > AirPlay, next to Screen saver, for the AirPlay receiver
this build ships (org.lineageos.tv.airplay): its switch; the name iPhones
and Macs show, which opens the device rename; a "New devices" page choosing
between asking for a code and not, with what each means spelled out; and
the paired devices, each opening a page to forget it, plus "Forget all"
when there are several.

The receiver's app keeps all of this. The page reads and changes it only
through that app's settings provider and its service, as the launcher's
Streaming tile does, so the two never disagree, and it observes the
provider's URI to follow changes made elsewhere while it is open: from the
tile, from adb, or from a device pairing. The row is hidden on a build
without the receiver.

In the two-panel layout, going back from a sub-page leaves that page in
the preview panel, so after a device was forgotten the preview went on
offering to forget it while the focus was on the next one. Rebuilding the
device list now asks the two-panel fragment to refresh the preview.

Change-Id: I353a04f008b7c7dfef4b34f127f0302301480d1b
